user: What intelligence! What month of the year has 28 days?
assistant: February is the only month of the year with 28 days. However, in leap years there are 29 days in February. Leap years are years lasting 366 days instead of 365 days for common years. Years are generally leap years if they are multiples of four, however they are not if they are multiples of one hundred with the exception of years multiples of four hundred which are leap years. This kind of year exists to compensate for the time difference between the common calendar year (365 days) and the solar year - the solar year (or tropical year) being the time taken by the Earth to complete one revolution around the Sun, which is 365.2422 days.
user: How many days are there in a leap year?
assistant: A leap year has 366 days, this is one day more than a regular year, since in leap years the month of February has one more day, resulting in this difference.
