Another goal could be to expand the business, take over competing clubs, or open new clubs in other areas and cities. Note that this goal is not always combined with the previous one, i.e. with increasing profits. 

Another goal is social, say, to guarantee good working conditions for all employees, or to provide access to a computer to those in need, even if they cannot pay the full price. Or maybe the club owner will help in the education of children and adults in his city, inviting them to master classes and lessons. Achieving such goals can improve a business's reputation and attract new customers and employees. In any case, it is good if there are numerical indicators by which you can determine whether the goal has been achieved or not.

